ml_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/13516#issuecomment-1542556548","id":1542556548,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/13516","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M5b8YuE","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1542556548/reactions"},"updated_at":"2023-05-10T17:22:07Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1542556548","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87458719?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monorimet/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monorimet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monorimet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monorimet/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monorimet","id":87458719,"login":"monorimet","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NDU4NzE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monorimet/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monorimet/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monorimet/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monorimet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monorimet/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monorimet","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"The only buffers we should be allocating host local/device visible are staging buffers and the only ones host visible/device local are external buffers (results from invocations, today) - all others (constants, variables, and transient memory) should be device local only. You can compile to the stream dialect and see if there's anything that stands out with your resource (`iree-compile --compile-to=stream`). If you can share a dump of that here I can see if I can spot anything obvious.","created_at":"2023-05-10T17:26:48Z","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/13516#issuecomment-1542562265","id":1542562265,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/13516","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M5b8aHZ","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":1,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":1,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1542562265/reactions"},"updated_at":"2023-05-10T17:26:48Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1542562265","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75337?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benvanik","id":75337,"login":"benvanik","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MzM3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87458719?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monorimet/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monorimet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monorimet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monorimet/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monorimet","id":87458719,"login":"monorimet","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NDU4NzE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monorimet/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monorimet/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monorimet/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monorimet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monorimet/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monorimet","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"### What happened?\n\nWith a device whose VRAM and memory heaps should be plenty sufficient for this allocation:\r\n```\r\nRuntimeError: Error registering modules: C:\\E\\SHARK-Runtime\\runtime\\src\\iree\\hal\\drivers\\vulkan\\vma_allocator.cc:693: RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED; VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY; vmaCreateBuffer; failed to allocate buffer of length 26953666560; while invoking native function hal.allocator.allocate.initialized; while calling import;\r\n[ 1]   native hal.allocator.allocate.initialized:0 -\r\n[ 0] bytecode module@1:2938 -\r\n```\r\nThe resource allocation issue seems to be happening because the HAL allocator gets the wrong memory type (DEVICE_VISIBLE over DEVICE_LOCAL) when trying to set up the buffer allocation.\r\n\r\nHere I show that the 26GB buffer can allocate successfully if the DEVICE_LOCAL memory type is explicitly specified:\r\n```\r\n(Pdb) config.device.allocator.allocate_buffer(memory_type=ireert.MemoryType.DEVICE_VISIBLE,allowed_usage=ireert.BufferUsage.DEFAULT,allocation_size=26953666560)\r\n*** RuntimeError: could not allocate buffer: D:\\a\\SHARK-Runtime\\SHARK-Runtime\\c\\runtime\\src\\iree\\hal\\drivers\\vulkan\\vma_allocator.cc:693: RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED; VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY; vmaCreateBuffer\r\n\r\n(Pdb) config.device.allocator.allocate_buffer(memory_type=ireert.MemoryType.DEVICE_LOCAL,allowed_usage=ireert.BufferUsage.DEFAULT,allocation_size=26953666560)\r\n<HalBuffer 26953666560 bytes (at offset 0 into 26953666560), memory_type=DEVICE_LOCAL, allowed_access=ALL, allowed_usage=TRANSFER|DISPATCH_STORAGE>\r\n```\r\nI put a few return_on_error prints in iree/hal/drivers/vulkan/vma_allocator.cc to see which memory type is specified for the failing allocation and it is always DEVICE_VISIBLE for w7900 in the stack below ireert.VmModule.from_flatbuffer() where we load the .vmfb into device memory in SHARK.\r\n\r\nCan this be explicitly changed on the python level or will it require refinement of the vma_allocator memory type populating?\r\nCan we specify the memory type or have it inferred from a compile-time option? I tried getting the right case to happen [in StreamToHAL](https://github.com/openxla/iree/blob/4d6c2b8699383598817352f19b5888b38be06ccb/compiler/src/iree/compiler/Dialect/HAL/Conversion/StreamToHAL/Patterns.cpp#L187) by compiling the .vmfb with `--iree-execution-model=async-external` but didn't see an effect on the inferred memory type. \r\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce your issue\n\n_No response_\n\n### What component(s) does this issue relate to?\n\nRuntime\n\n### Version information\n\n[5b89a14](https://github.com/openxla/iree/commit/5b89a145d02fcad42cd375b7ae447bfd672471af)\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_","closed_at":null,"closed_by":null,"comments":4,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/13516/comments","created_at":"2023-05-10T11:20:10Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/13516/events","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/13516","id":1703698411,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"d73a4a","default":false,"description":"Something isn't working","id":1553038945,"name":"bug 🐞","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNTUzMDM4OTQ1","u